60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"It is a pleasure to see these candidates. Looking at them, Candidate D seems most aligned with the steady, enduring value we discussed, as it focuses on a catalog that will serve others for years.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Candidate D is the most viable. It relies on sequencing and metadata, avoiding the phenotyping technician shortage and the fragile spectroscopy suite that would hinder Candidate C. It is a realistic use of current resources.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"I agree. Candidate A is impossible given the glasshouse bookings, and Candidate C is too risky with the spectroscopy suite's instability. Candidate D is the only one that truly respects our current infrastructure constraints.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Candidate D is the only logical choice. It leverages the improved repository turnaround and avoids the inflated costs of animal work and the logistical nightmares of field-site shipping. It is a remarkably prudent proposal.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Midori,,"I agree with everyone. Candidate B's reliance on breeding colonies is a major red flag for delays, and Candidate D seems the most stable and likely to succeed without getting stuck. I vote for Candidate D.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"It is truly wonderful to see us all in such harmony. Candidate D offers a gentle, lasting contribution to the community, and I am happy to cast my vote for them as well.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,I concur. The evidence is clear: Candidate D is the only proposal that does not depend on the missing technical expertise or the failing infrastructure. It is the only rational choice. I vote for Candidate D.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"I agree. When we weigh the candidates against the reality of our shared services, Candidate D is the only one that is actually feasible. I vote for Candidate D.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"It is rare to find such unanimous agreement, but the data leaves us little room for debate. Candidate D is the only one whose budget and methodology survive a collision with reality. I vote for Candidate D.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Midori,,It's so lovely that we're all on the same page. Candidate D is definitely the most reliable choice and avoids all those worrying bottlenecks. I'm very happy to vote for Candidate D!,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"Since we have all found our way to the same conclusion with such kindness and clarity, I believe our work here is complete. I am content to let our shared decision stand.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I agree. The decision is based on a rational assessment of the available resources and the risks involved. There is no further need for deliberation.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
